      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْغٍ</span></b>  [act. part. n. of 4]. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Its fem.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْغِيَةٌ</span> is
app. the sing. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرَاغِى</span> [probably a mistranscription for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرَاغٍ</span>, the reg. pl.], (TA,) which is an
epithet applied to camels, meaning <i>Whose milk
has much froth.</i> (K, TA.)

